{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And the people.</b> Concerning Israel." "<b>Who strikes him.</b> It is HaShem, for He is the one who strikes [מכ'] in truth, and the signs [indicate] two, as in 'in the midst of the tents' (Joshua 7:21)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {1 "מכ' resolved as מכה; 'the signs [indicate] two' refers to the Masoretic accents or plural forms, following Ibn Ezra's standard terminology; the hyper-literal rendering preserves the compressed syntax."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:01.682327916Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}